{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>He is unclean; the priest shall pronounce him unclean.</b> And similarly it stated above, ״He is clean; the priest shall pronounce him clean.״ It is a scriptural decree that impurity and purity be by the mouth of the priest, and it teaches you that even though the priest has seen in the affliction the signs of purity or impurity, he must pronounce from his mouth ״clean״ or ״unclean.״ <br>And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: this is one of the matters on account of which Hillel went up from Babylonia — that is, he went up to the Sages of the Land of Israel to know the reason for the matter."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:14.014903555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}